  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Consists of 22 cards of photographic images printed with captions on backs of cards, issued in a portfolio within a slipcase. Ink-jet printed on 167 gm. Epson Matte paper.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"All images are by Ral Veroni except 'Cranes' by Guido Indij ... In an edition of 50, each copy is numbered and signed by the artist"--Index.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"[This work] reflects on this city of immigrants and their daily struggle for survival. For this project, made during 2000 and 2001, Ral Veroni resorted to the strategy of the flaneur: long walks around town with no predetermined aim, taking photographs and notes about the city, its architecture and its neighborhoods. The insertion of emblematic figures - representing time, destiny, desire - in the cityscape create a subtle mix of metaphors. These images not only refer to the ups and downs of human existence but also, depending on the landmarks where these symbols are placed, to the complex political and social problems of the country. "--Vamp &amp; Tramp website, accessed 4/24/2012.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
